{% psec 1, "From a Gas Curve to a Credit Rating", "What was the brief?", "Overview" %}
<p class="topic-intro">
  Four tasks from J.P. Morgan's Quantitative Research job simulation. The first two sit on a commodities desk: build a natural gas price curve, then price a storage contract with it. The last two sit with the credit risk team: predict which borrowers will default, then turn FICO scores into a rating scale. I rebuilt the curve and the default model from scratch, extended the other two, and tested every model on data it hadn't seen.
</p>
