<div class="sh">In plain words</div>
<p class="np">Natural gas is cheap in summer and dear in winter, because that's when people heat their homes. If you rent a storage tank, you can <strong>buy gas in summer, keep it, and sell it in winter</strong>. Whether that makes money depends on two things: how big the price gap is, and how much the tank costs to rent while you wait. The second half of the project asks a lender's question instead: <strong>who won't pay us back, and how much will that cost?</strong></p>

